So in this question we were given three arrays main array and two arrays to get the starting and last index to get the query range.
You are given an array of n integers, nums, and two arrays of m integers each, l and r, representing the m range queries, where the ith query is the range [l[i], r[i]]. All the arrays are 0-indexed.
Return a list of boolean elements answer, where answer[i] is true if the subarray nums[l[i]], nums[l[i]+1], ... , nums[r[i]] can be rearranged to form an arithmetic sequence, and false otherwise.
So I did a question where I had to check if an array is ap or not I used the logic here to check if the given range query is ap or not .
First by sorting the array and then finding  the common difference between the first two elements in the range and then checking the common difference 
For all the remaining elements in the range query.
The main problem was How I would sort the array for a certain given range I searched it up and it is done by.
sort(v.begin()+low,v.end()+end +1)
now it was done I also made the mistake that I was sorting the main array each time that changed the order for the range queries.
I fixed it by making a copy of the main array and then sorting the index query range after I checked for that range.
I gave the original value back to the main array.
class Solution {
public:
    vector<bool> checkArithmeticSubarrays(vector<int>& nums, vector<int>& l, vector<int>& r) {
        vector<bool> v;
        int start = 0;
        int end = 0;
        for(int i = 0;i<l.size();i++){
            start = l[i];
            end = r[i];
            vector <int> backup = nums;
            int count = 0;
            sort(nums.begin() + start, nums.begin() + end +1);
            int d = nums[start+1]-nums[start];
            for(int j = l[i];j<end;j++){
                if(nums[j+1]-nums[j]!=d){
                    v.push_back(false);
                    count++;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if(count==0){
                v.push_back(true);
            }
            nums = backup;
        }
        return v;
    }
};


